course: dictionary
lesson: 14355
title: Omission: the word that is missing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An omission is something that has been left out or not done. The word comes from the verb omit, which means to leave something out. When a word or step is missing, an omission has happened. Look at the clues around the gap to find out what is missing.
explain: «The shopping list was good, but it had one big omission: nobody had written down the milk.» The sentence tells you the list is missing something. The milk is what was left out, so an omission is a gap where something should be.
explain: Writers use an apostrophe of omission to show letters that have been left out. «Don't» is short for «do not», and the apostrophe shows where the o has gone. «Can't» is short for «cannot». Look for the apostrophe, then ask: which letters are missing?
explain: In maths, leaving out a step in your working is also an omission. Your teacher can only see how you reached your answer if every step is there. A serious omission might lose you marks, even when your final answer is right.
fact: An omission is something that has been left out or not done.
fact: Omission is a noun. Its verb is omit, meaning to leave something out.
fact: An apostrophe of omission shows missing letters, as in «can't» for «cannot».
fact: A serious omission is a big thing left out, such as a player missing from a team list.
fact: Leaving out a step in your working is an omission, and it can cost you marks.
exercise: «The team list had a serious omission: the captain's name was not on it.» What is the omission? | The name of the coach | The final score | The date of the match | *The captain's name, which was left out
exercise: In «don't», what has been left out? | *The letter o, from «do not» | The letter n | The letter d | The whole word «not»
exercise: Sam solved a maths problem but missed out a step in the working. What has Sam made? | *An omission | A question | A compliment | A rhyme
test: «Lily found an omission in her essay: she had left out the ending.» What does omission mean here? | A large, shiny hat | A type of bird | *Something that has been left out | Something added twice
test: Which sentence shows an apostrophe of omission? | The park is big and green. | Ben, Sara and Tom are here. | *I can't come to the park today. | Where are my boots?
exam: «The team list had a big omission: Jake was not on it.» What does big omission mean? | A new team shirt | A winning goal | *Something important that was left out | A large crowd of fans
